<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9158"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 11:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->taken from <a href="http://www.arkvalleynews.com" target=_top>www.arkvalleynews.com</a> <BR> <BR>Jan. 28, 2005--Jeff Magness reported a large dog fell into his basement window well and possibly was injured at 1727 E. Broadbeck. Compliance Officer Dennis Rader removed the dog without incident, Officer Hobert Capps reported. <BR> <BR>Aug. 26, 2004--Officer Dwight Wilkes reported assisting Dennis Rader and the county fire department with a very small fire at 6401 N.W. Parkview. <BR> <BR>July 18, 2004--Officers Michael Kingsford and Dwight Wilkes assisted Dennis Rader in taking a pit bull into custody. The animal had bitten a person at 7530 N. Hydraulic earlier in the day. <BR> <BR>June 13, 2004 --Officer Timothy Dye responded to the report of a stray white, black and brown pit bull in the area of the 6500 block of East Parkview. The animal was impounded by Dennis Rader. <BR> <BR>April 13, 2004 --Officer Michael Kingsford assisted Compliance Officer Dennis Rader with an injured opossum in the 1000 block of East Evanston. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1022789734420~dennis" target=_top>http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1022789 734420~dennis</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1010093761803~dennis" target=_top>http://www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll?1010093 761803~dennis</a> <BR> <BR>According to that last article, Dennis was taken to the hospital<!--/Text--></td></tr>
