<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9166"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Verm, <BR> <BR>It looks like it was a jeep accident in CO. that claimed the life of Michelle. <BR> <BR>Wichita Eagle 8/30/69 <BR> <BR>Steve_huff, <BR> <BR>You are a stud. The City of Industry is about 40 minutes drive from Santa Monica. <BR> <BR>CV in CA<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9166-->
<!--Post: 9174--><!--Time: 1109407720-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9174"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another California Connection: On his daughter&#39;s website are links to family and friends. One link is to a family homepage. It must be of a cousin to Dennis Rader. It&#39;s the website of James L. Rader of Rancho Cordova, California. He graduated from Apple Valley, Californai High School in 1960, worked as a surveyor for CalTrans, was an investment officer, a programmer analyst and a teacher. A computer wiz and genealogist. Close enough to the Raders of Wichita that Dennis Rader&#39;s daughter links to his website so you could assume that Dennis Rader would visit this relative in California. Another opportunity to send communications from the City of Industry, California to Wichita,<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9174-->
<!--Post: 9179--><!--Time: 1109408796-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9179"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 1:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Steve_huff, <BR> <BR>You are a stud...&#34; <BR> <BR>And can I quote you on that? :^&#41; <BR> <BR>Since I&#39;m the father of 4 children, my wife may agree with you.  <BR> <BR>Seriously, thanks. I have also, very sporadically, received hits on my <a href="http://www.planethuff.com/darkside">blog</a> from Kinko&#39;s located in California - one was about 9 miles from Industry&#39;s city limits. I&#39;m convinced Denny the Dog Catcher was taking the really anonymous route, checking up on his publicity in a seemingly out-of-the-way locale.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9179-->
<!--Post: 9182--><!--Time: 1109411067-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9182"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 1:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno- <BR> <BR>I live very close to James Radar, and let me tell you, almost anywhere else in the U.S. Rancho Cordova / Sacramento and The City of Industry would be in different states, and even might have a whole other state in between them!  They are over 400 miles apart. <a href="http://www.mapquest.com/directions/main.adp?go=1&amp;do=nw&amp;un=m&amp;cl=EN&amp;ct=NA&amp;rsres=1&amp;1y=US&amp;1a=&amp;1c=rancho%2Bcordova&amp;1s=CA&amp;1z=&amp;2y=US&amp;2a=&amp;2c=city%2Bof%2Bindustry&amp;2s=CA&amp;2z=" target=_top>http://www.mapquest.com/directions/main.adp?go=1&amp;d o=nw&amp;un=m&amp;cl=EN&amp;ct=NA&amp;rsres=1&amp;1y=US&amp;1a=&amp;1c=rancho&#43; cordova&amp;1s=CA&amp;1z=&amp;2y=US&amp;2a=&amp;2c=city&#43;of&#43;industry&amp;2s =CA&amp;2z=</a>  I doubt BTK would make a 5 to 6 hour raod trip just to send a letter.  That&#39;s not to say BKT didn&#39;t indeed mail this correspondence, just that visiting James was not his opportunity to do so. <BR> <BR>BTW: <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/10/464.html?1108170438" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/10/464.htm l?1108170438</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9182-->
<!--Post: 9188--><!--Time: 1109415225-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9188"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 2:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Park City local news columnist reported in September 2004 that Dennis Rader received an award for 10 years of service.  Wonder what he did before that? <BR> <BR><a href="http://64.233.161.104/search?q=cache:MPU0WKHnRqAJ:www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll%3F1002231221345%2B%2B%22Dennis%2BRader%22&amp;hl=en&amp;ie=UTF-8" target=_top>http://64.233.161.104/search?q=cache:MPU0WKHnRqAJ: www.arkvalleynews.com/web/isite.dll%3F100223122134 5&#43;&#43;%22Dennis&#43;Rader%22&amp;hl=en&amp;ie=UTF-8</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9188-->
<!--Post: 9209--><!--Time: 1109429891-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9209"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jilleng<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jilleng<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 6:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->check out this link...appears he was also on the zoning commission <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/countyclerk/1996/regular/reg04-10.pdf" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/countyclerk/1996/reg ular/reg04-10.pdf</a> <BR> <BR>Check under &#34;guests&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9209-->
<!--Post: 9244--><!--Time: 1109444024-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9244"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 10:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very good work all of you !!!...Now we know ...but was Denny responsible for any other murders..and what other nonmurder mischief did he do..especially in that church..child molestation, embezzlement..what else ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9244-->
<!--Post: 9247--><!--Time: 1109445276-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9247"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 11:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think we should stick to the guy himself. Dig up everything on him, but leave the relatives out of it. They are already embarassed enough. Think about how Brian Rader feels right now. As to him driving to Rancho to use another Kinko&#39;s while visiting his possible relative. He would not have used a Kinko&#39;s here in the Sacramento area, if indeed that is his relative. Somewhere along the way, but he was smart enough to have sent from Industry, which really could not have been connected to his son in Santa Monica. It is interesting to note that this supposed cousin here in Rancho lives only 4 blocks from 2 confirmed East Area Rapist attacks. It really is a small world. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9247-->
<!--Post: 9248--><!--Time: 1109445720-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9248"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 11:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Per news reports this morning Rader worked as an ADT Technician and spent 4 years in the Air Force. Neither of these items are from confirmed sources though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9248-->
<!--Post: 9250--><!--Time: 1109446489-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9250"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 11:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->QUESTION: What the heck is an &#34;ADT Technician&#34;?? I&#39;ve heard this all over the &#39;boards&#39;, but what in blazes does it mean?! <BR> <BR> What were his duties &amp; skills there?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9250-->
<!--Post: 9252--><!--Time: 1109446663-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9252"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Isleuth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Isleuth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 11:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It would be interesting to see a pic of what he looked like in the 70s &#40;to see how close any of the sketches were.&#41;   <BR> <BR>Also it will be great, as more details come to light, to start a &#39;lessons learned&#39; thread based on where we were on the right track or not. This will help a lot in catching other serial killers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9252-->
<!--Post: 9253--><!--Time: 1109448424-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9253"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rader worked for Coleman. Just as all of us had suspected all along. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansascity.com/mld/kansascity/11000933.htm?1c" target=_top>http://www.kansascity.com/mld/kansascity/11000933. htm?1c</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9253-->
<!--Post: 9254--><!--Time: 1109448803-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9254"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->An ADT technician installs and services alarm systems of all types. ADT is a nationwide company. Someone please come up with his Air Force service record, including exact unit number. My guess as to date would be from 1964 upward, either 4 or more years. It would be interesting to see him stationed here in Northern California. That might explain how his actions mimicked those of Zodiac, he was right here observing it first hand. <BR>Isleuth: your idea is a great one. I can&#39;t see it not being done. I will be among those contributing, probably one of fifty or more. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9254-->
<!--Post: 9255--><!--Time: 1109448848-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9255"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Vscantu, As far as I know, ADT is a home security alarm company. It could be something else, but I am assuming the ADT tech would be the person to install home security systems. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9255-->
<!--Post: 9256--><!--Time: 1109449387-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9256"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ADT is a security firm, house alarms, etc. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9256-->
<!--Post: 9257--><!--Time: 1109450688-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9257"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marga<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marga<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 12:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->more recent photo of Rader? <BR><a href="http://www.comcast.net/News/DOMESTIC//XML/1110_AP_Online_Regional___National__US_/3cbb251b-dff8-40ea-a859-dd2fba9be3c7.html" target=_top>http://www.comcast.net/News/DOMESTIC//XML/1110_AP_ Online_Regional___National__US_/3cbb251b-dff8-40ea -a859-dd2fba9be3c7.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9257-->
<!--Post: 9261--><!--Time: 1109452657-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9261"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Marga<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Marga<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 1:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good link with video of Rader: <BR><a href="http://ksn.com/news/stories/7036051.html" target=_top>http://ksn.com/news/stories/7036051.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9261-->
<!--Post: 9266--><!--Time: 1109458037-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9266"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 2:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it possible that there are california victims? I&#39;ve seen several posts about a brother in california, I just assume that he visted him. This guy could be a prolific serial killer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9266-->
<!--Post: 9281--><!--Time: 1109460586-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9281"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 3:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wegerle and Fox both attended or had connections to St. Andrew&#39;s Lutheran Church, right?  D.R. was recently involved with Christ Lutheran Church.  Anyone taking bets as to whether D.R. was associated with St. Andrew&#39;s back in the 70&#39;s and 80&#39;s?!?  Did the Rader&#39;s live near Wegerle and was he the source of the &#34;no one&#39;s hitting the panic button&#34; quote that was in the paper?!?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9281-->
<!--Post: 9282--><!--Time: 1109461686-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9282"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 3:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Apparently in the 70&#39;s he did work at Coleman like two of the victims did ...  <BR> <BR>Also,  since he went to wichita state U.  Then perhaps some of those unfortunate WSU students are his wrok as well <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/sad.gif" ALT=":-&#40;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9282-->
<!--Post: 9300--><!--Time: 1109465546-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9300"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 4:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am waitingfor the police to link himto the other murders in Pary City, the one&#39;s where the Victims were left on the side of the road, or under bridges. I honestly do not believe he stopped killing all that time, and it sounds like he made sure he had jobs where he could be out observing people all day, I am still assuming he knew Joe Otero from the military, I am trying to dig up his military records from the Air Force.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9300-->
