<!--Post: 9494--><!--Time: 1109539046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9494"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 1:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was pretty close on his Air Force record. 1965-1969, Stationed in Korea, Turkey, Greece, and Okinawa. Looks like he joined to avoid being drafted into the Army, that&#39;s just about when his number could have come up.  <BR>One thing I don&#39;t get yet is that the Rader in Sacramento graduated from Apple Valley High School in California in 1960. Where does that place him in the family tree?  <BR>As to the contacts to your blog, Mr. Huff, the letter that was postmarked Industry could really have been dropped in a box right outside the Kinko&#39;s that he sent the messages from. Mail is picked up from boxes and satelite stations and sent to processing centers for cancellation and consolidation. It seems very likely he was visiting his son when he did that. Did he pass through Sacramento to visit his other relative on the way home? Maybe, not known yet.  <BR>As far as him committing any crimes in his travels, I don&#39;t think he did any out here in California. The idea of tying him to the Cabin 28 murders in 1981 in Keddie is just too much woo-woo for me. After Otero, it&#39;s my hunch that he only did his thing within about a 200 mile radius of Wichita, maybe even less. As to what he might have done while in, who knows? That stuff is kept kinda quiet. You have to find people who served with him. Look at Yates. Some people who were on that base in Germany with him have some juicy stories to tell. I&#39;d look first at any old cases unsolved in the areas he was in between 1969-70 and the time of Otero. Just a crazy hunch.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9494-->
<!--Post: 9498--><!--Time: 1109539348-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9498"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 1:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Family tree &#40;don&#39;t think this has been posted&#41;: <BR> <BR><a href="http://66.102.7.104/search?q=cache:0MJ1HZyQOfAJ:familytree.paradigmpress.net/f_25f.htm%2B%22Paul%2BRader%22%2BDennis%2BWichita&amp;hl=en&amp;start=7" target=_top>http://66.102.7.104/search?q=cache:0MJ1HZyQOfAJ:fa milytree.paradigmpress.net/f_25f.htm&#43;%22Paul&#43;Rader %22&#43;Dennis&#43;Wichita&amp;hl=en&amp;start=7</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9498-->
<!--Post: 9504--><!--Time: 1109540860-->
