<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9506"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 1:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After further inspection of the records, it becomes quite obvious that The James L. Rader of Rancho Cordova Ca has no direct connection to Dennis Rader. This person&#39;s geanology traces from San Bernardino area to Washington and La Crosse Wisconsin. Absolutely no connection to Kansas.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
