<!--Post: 9513--><!--Time: 1109542950-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9513"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 2:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;...The idea of tying him to the Cabin 28 murders in 1981 in Keddie is just too much woo-woo for me...&#34; <BR> <BR>I&#39;m in total agreement. If you want to connect the guy, try and find unsolved crimes that make sense. He didn&#39;t vary his MO THAT much, apparently. Abducted Hedge and Davis, appears to be the biggest change he made.  <BR> <BR>BTK didn&#39;t like blood and gore. He liked the death itself. He rarely stabbed or shot. He preferred strangling. The Keddie murders were horrifically bloody, by all accounts. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9513-->
