<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9784"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would like to be the first one to point out that I was wrong! <BR> <BR>In prior posts regarding the investigation I stated several times that BTK would not be caught by &#34;slipping up&#34;. I am happy to admit that I was wrong. As everyone knows by now, it was a very big &#34;boo boo&#34; on his part that gave LE his true identity. All they had to do after that was fill in the blanks, which with the DNA, prints, voice recordings and his personal history didn&#39;t seem to be much of a task. <BR> <BR>Also, curious about your theories&#39; regarding the DNA; how it was obtained and from whom. It just seems strange that at first it was reported that the DNA came from his daughter everybody assumed that she turned him in. Now that theory has been shot down, then we find out the DNA was not from a blood sample, but from a strand of hair, hmmmm. <BR> <BR>My guess is that either his wife or one of his inlaws had the daughter&#39;s brush and gave it to LE. <BR> <BR>My theory: <BR> <BR>-Cops find name on floppy &#40;Hmmm, let&#39;s check this dude&#41; <BR>-Start to follow him  <BR>-Work up a history &#40;Could Be&#41; <BR>-While following him observe him using payphone &#40;Kinda strange, most people have cell phone&#41; <BR>-Find out he used the phone to call KAKE anchorman &#40;Whoa!&#41; <BR>-Get prints from phone &#40;Lookin Good&#41; <BR>-Contact In-Laws, get strand of hair <BR>-Compare voice sample, from old TV footage &#40;Lookin Real Good!&#41;  <BR>-Observe car on security tapes at Home Depot &#40;That&#39;s Strange he was there too?&#41; <BR>-Get DNA results back &#40;Holy Schmidt!&#41; <BR>-Search the house &#40;Hey, that look familiar&#41; <BR> <BR>Any thought? <BR> <BR>iq <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
