<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9846"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 10:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Want to put a family perspective on this sicko? <BR> <BR>His son is born on July 27, 1975. Nine months before his birth on October 22, 1974 the first confirmed BTK communication is recieved in a phone call to a TIPS hotline informing them of the letter in the book in the library that claims responsibility to the Otero murders. <BR> <BR>His daughter is born June 13, 1978. During his wife&#39;s pregnancy the Fox murder is committed in December 1977, The &#39;Shirley Locks&#39; poem is recieved in January 1978 printed on an index card from a childs printing block set and in February 1978 the &#39;Oh! Death to Nancy&#39; Poem is recieved in the same communication where he names himself BTK. <BR> <BR>Two days after his daughter&#39;s first birthday the letter to Anna Wiiliams is recieved on June 15, 1979 containing the Oh Death to Anna poem. <BR> <BR>March 17, 1977 on the day after his niece Andrea&#39;s third birthday Shirley Vian his slain. Her children spared. <BR> <BR>March 17, 2004 on the day after his niece Andrea&#39;s 30th birthday the Bill Thomas Killman letter is mailed. <BR> <BR>December 14, 2004 on his nephew Jason&#39;s 30th birthday the Murdock Park package is found.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
