<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10004"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 4:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No offense, but I don&#39;t think the family tree is connected to this Dennis Rader, look: <BR> <BR>This is an excerpt from an interview with his brother Jeff. <BR> <BR>Jeff Rader is a plumber, 50, nine years younger. Unlike his balding older brother, he&#39;s got a full head of hair, brown and curly. <BR> <BR>The four brothers &#40;Dennis is the eldest&#41; grew up with a loving mother and a tough but decent father, he said. <BR> <BR>Their father, William Rader, was a former Marine, a God-fearing man, strict but not unreasonable. He died in 1996. <BR> <BR>This shows that Dennis &#40;BTK&#41; is the oldest and his father&#39;s name was William. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
